HGSS on the PC: SoulSilver in the same build as HeartGold (ss1, 2026-11-14). pret picks the version with a define
(GAME_VERSION, HEARTGOLD / SOULSILVER: include/config.h, 13 `#ifdef HEARTGOLD` sites, the GBA-migrator table in
asm/overlay_74_thumb.s). The two ROMs have the same file system (soulsilver.us/filesystem.csv differs from heartgold.us' by
two file names, same ids), so the version is a value the PC build reads when it runs: gGameVersion (pm_version.c, not const),
set by the table of the game that starts (port/game/game_table.c: hg_bwgame IPKE, ss_bwgame IPGE) before NitroMain.
GAME_VERSION is gGameVersion for C (config.h), GAME_IS_HEARTGOLD the test; each site that chose with HEARTGOLD or SOULSILVER
chooses with it. Sorts last, made against the pin + every other patch. DROP when upstream makes the version a value.
Handover-ID: none (port-only)

